+**Background work with nobody watching.** A `terminal(background=true,
+notify_on_complete=true)` process that exits while its CLI, TUI or Desktop
+session has no viewer is written into the session as a note, and the next turn
+reads it. To have the agent pick the work back up on its own, set
+`sessions.unviewed_completion_turns` to the number of such exits a session may
+run as agent turns in a row with no viewer (default `0`: notes only):
+
+```yaml
+sessions:
+  unviewed_completion_turns: 20
+```
+
+The turn runs and is saved like any other, so a client that attaches later
+sees it in the history. A viewer attaching or a message from you starts the
+count again (so does a gateway restart); past the limit, exits are notes until
+then. A chat you closed (exit or `/new`) keeps notes. A session the gateway
+ended because its viewer vanished is reopened for the turn and ended again
+`sessions.orphan_end_grace_s` after the turn starts, or when it settles if
+that is later. Watch-pattern notices and background
+subagent results are not affected, and neither are messaging chats, whose
+completions always start a turn.
+
